<!DOCTYPE html>
<html class="no-js" lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

  <title>
    {%- if page_title -%}
      {{ page_title }}
      {%- if current_tags %} &ndash; tagged "{{ current_tags | join: ', ' }}"{% endif -%}
      {%- if current_page != 1 %} &ndash; Page {{ current_page }}{% endif -%}
      {%- unless page_title contains shop.name %} &ndash; {{ shop.name }}{% endunless -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {{ shop.name }}
    {%- endif -%}
  </title>

  {%- if page_description -%}
    <meta name="description" content="{{ page_description | escape }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">

  {%- comment -%}
    Open Graph / Twitter. Shopify's content_for_header already injects the
    og:image family, so only the rest is declared here — without og:title and
    og:description a shared link showed a picture and the bare URL.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign og_title = page_title | default: shop.name
    assign og_description = page_description | default: shop.description | default: shop.name
    assign og_type = 'website'
    case request.page_type
      when 'product'
        assign og_type = 'product'
      when 'article'
        assign og_type = 'article'
    endcase
  -%}
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ shop.name | escape }}">
  <meta property="og:url" content="{{ canonical_url }}">
  <meta property="og:title" content="{{ og_title | escape }}">
  <meta property="og:type" content="{{ og_type }}">
  <meta property="og:description" content="{{ og_description | escape }}">

  {%- comment -%}
    Share image. Shopify's own og:image falls back to the theme logo, which is
    an SVG — and Facebook, LinkedIn, iMessage and Slack will not render SVG, so
    a shared page previewed with no image at all. Product and collection pages
    were already fine; pages were not.

    Resolved most specific first: the page's own custom.share_image metafield,
    then the theme's default. Emitted before content_for_header so this tag is
    the first og:image in the document, which is the one crawlers take.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign share_image = blank
    case request.page_type
      when 'product'
        assign share_image = product.featured_image
      when 'collection'
        assign share_image = collection.image
      when 'page'
        assign share_image = page.metafields.custom.share_image.value
    endcase
    if share_image == blank
      assign share_image = settings.share_image
    endif
  -%}
  {%- if share_image != blank -%}
    {%- assign share_image_url = share_image | image_url: width: 1200 -%}
    <meta property="og:image" content="https:{{ share_image_url }}">
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="https:{{ share_image_url }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  <meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ og_title | escape }}">
  <meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ og_description | escape }}">

  {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 32, height: 32 }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} Google Fonts: Instrument Serif (display) + Bricolage Grotesque (UI / body) {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&family=Bricolage+Grotesque:wght@400;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

  <style>
    :root {
      /* Brand Vol. 01 (2026) — cobalt/editorial. Chalk/Bone light, Ink text, Cobalt ground, Butter/Coral accents */
      --warm-white: {{ settings.color_warm_white }};   /* Chalk — light page bg */
      --sand: {{ settings.color_sand }};               /* Bone — secondary light / text on dark */
      --clay: {{ settings.color_clay }};               /* Butter — pop accent */
      --accent: {{ settings.color_accent }};           /* Coral — links, eyebrows, details */
      --charcoal: {{ settings.color_charcoal }};       /* Ink — primary text + deep grounds */
      --mid: {{ settings.color_mid }};                 /* Cobalt — signature ground */
      --cobalt: {{ settings.color_mid }};              /* alias for signature ground */
      --font-heading: '{{ settings.heading_font_family | default: "Bricolage Grotesque" }}', sans-serif;
      --font-body: '{{ settings.body_font_family | default: "Bricolage Grotesque" }}', sans-serif;
      --font-display: 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif;
      --logo-max-width: {{ settings.logo_max_width | default: 140 }}px;
    }
  </style>

  {{ 'base.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  {{ content_for_header }}

  {%- comment -%} Prevent FOUC {%- endcomment -%}
  <script>document.documentElement.className = document.documentElement.className.replace('no-js', 'js');</script>
</head>

<body class="template-{{ template.name }}{% if template.suffix %} template-{{ template.name }}-{{ template.suffix }}{% endif %}">
  <a class="skip-to-content" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

  {% sections 'header-group' %}

  <main id="main" role="main">
    {{ content_for_layout }}
  </main>

  {% sections 'footer-group' %}

  <script src="{{ 'theme.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
